{
  // Build-only configuration. `tsconfig.json` deliberately covers tests and
  // `vitest.config.ts` so `typecheck` checks them too, but including a file
  // outside `src/` widens the inferred common root to the repository root: every
  // emitted file moved down into `dist/src/`, which did not match the `bin` and
  // `exports` paths in package.json, and a compiled `vitest.config.js` shipped in
  // the build output alongside 153 compiled test files.
  //
  // `types` is explicit because the Node ambient types were reaching the program
  // only through `vitest.config.ts` importing `vitest/config`. Dropping that file
  // from the build silently removed `Buffer` and the `node:*` modules, so the
  // build was depending on a test configuration for its platform types.
  //
  // `sourceMap` is off for the published build. `tsconfig.json` turns it on, but
  // `files` in package.json ships `dist/` and `schema/` only, so every emitted
  // `.js.map` pointed at `../../../src/*.ts` paths that are absent from the
  // tarball: 249 maps, roughly half the unpacked size, that no debugger could
  // resolve. The alternatives were shipping `src/` or inlining the sources into
  // the maps; both pay real bytes for a package that is developed from a source
  // checkout, where `tsconfig.json` still emits working maps.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": "src",
    "types": ["node"],
    "sourceMap": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  // `src/shared/testing/` holds assertions shared BETWEEN test suites. Nothing at
  // runtime imports it, so shipping it in `dist/` would only add dead weight to
  // the published package.
  //
  // `reporting-fixture.ts` is the same thing under a different name: the report
  // fixture the four reporter suites share. It sits beside the domain rather
  // than in `shared/testing/`, so the rule above missed it and it was shipping.
  // Only `*.test.ts` files import it — an excluded file that a shipped module
  // imported would still be compiled in, so this exclusion drops it only
  // because nothing at runtime needs it.
  "exclude": [
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/shared/testing/**",
    "src/domains/reporting/reporting-fixture.ts",
    "src/domains/evaluation/change-impact-fixture.ts"
  ]
}
